  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 14,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "How to read this page",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 7
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "The journey-service stores every accepted scan as an **event in the outbox** (same transaction) and a **relay** sends the events to Kafka. Healthy means: *waiting* is 0 or small, the *oldest waiting* event is a few seconds old, *failed* and *parked* stay at 0, and *published* follows *scans ingested*.\n\n* **Waiting now** - events stored but not yet acknowledged by Kafka.\n* **Oldest waiting** - how long the oldest of them has waited. Growing means the relay is stuck or Kafka is down.\n* **Failed** - sends that failed and will be retried. **Parked** - events Kafka refused for good (needs a person).\n* **Publish delay** - time from storing an event until Kafka acknowledged it.\n* **Relay runs (traces)** - one row per run that had events; open it to see each Kafka send inside. *Runs that sent nothing* lists the runs that could not reach Kafka.\n\nThe messages themselves are in [Open Kafka UI](http://localhost:8090/ui/clusters/local/all-topics) (topic `baggage.scan.received.v1`)."
      }
    },
